   "text": {
    "L1": "First, Aditi's family travels up the hills by bus.",
    "L2": "Then the bus climbs higher, and the air becomes cold.",
    "L3": "They see a village with flags and a yak.",
    "L4": "At last, they reach the top of the pass and see snow-capped peaks shining in the sun.",
    "L5": "A peak is the pointed top of a mountain. A pass is a route through the mountains.",
    "L6": "Snow-capped means covered with snow on top, like a white cap on a head.",
    "L7": "The pine trees stood in rows like soldiers. They were not real soldiers; like shows a comparison.",
    "L8": "The mountains are home to people and animals, and rivers like the Ganga begin there."
   },
